{
  "id": "P10",
  "format": "posting-scenario/v1",
  "name": "A true half-way tie at the service-line rounding boundary: half-up, not half-even, not truncation",
  "rules": ["SALE_POSTED/service@1"],
  "source": "docs/posting-rules/service-sale.md §6",
  "governedBy": ["ADR-0011", "ADR-0014"],
  "executableFrom": "M3",
  "status": "Specified, hand-computed. Not yet executed: needs sales invoices (M3). Step 1 marked \"level\": \"kernel\" (Accounting seat ruling, 2026-09-29, review of the M3-Q throwaway verify against M3-P @efb7e3f): the real modules/receivables command has no lineNet field for a client to submit, so SALE_AMOUNT_MISMATCH is reachable only at the kernel, as P03 does. Step 2 (module-level) gains an `invoiceLines` assertion that the module independently computes the SAME half-up tie, 3086.4193 — the reason this scenario exists. No figure changed.",
  "description": [
    "Line 1: 2.500000 × 1234.567700 = 3086.41925 exactly — a tie at the 5th decimal.",
    "  half-up (ADR-0011, away from zero)  → 3086.4193   ← the only accepted value",
    "  half-even (banker's)                → 3086.4192   (4th digit 2 is even)",
    "  truncation                          → 3086.4192",
    "Line 2: 1.000000 × 13.580700 = 13.5807 exactly; no rounding occurs.",
    "netAmount = 3086.4193 + 13.5807 = 3100.0000",
    "",
    "Step 1 submits the half-even / truncated figure and must be rejected: the kernel",
    "verifies the module's arithmetic with the same Money function and never substitutes",
    "its own figure.",
    "",
    "Step 2 posts: Dr 1200 [CUST-A] 3100.0000 / Cr 4200 3100.0000. Both sides are built",
    "from the same rounded line nets, so no residual exists and the rounding account",
    "stays at 0.0000.",
    "",
    "Independently recomputed for M2-000 with decimal.js: 2.5 × 1234.5677 = 3086.41925;",
    "toDecimalPlaces(4, ROUND_HALF_UP) = 3086.4193; ROUND_HALF_EVEN = 3086.4192."
  ],
